---
import FAQ from '../FAQ.astro';
import { faqs as defaultFaqs, creatorTiers as defaultCreatorTiers, type CreatorTier, type FAQItem } from './calculatorData';

interface Props {
  creatorTiers?: CreatorTier[];
  faqs?: FAQItem[];
}

const { creatorTiers = defaultCreatorTiers, faqs = defaultFaqs } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="prose prose-sm md:prose-base prose-ink max-w-none space-y-16">
    
    {/* Section 1: What is Instagram Engagement Rate and Who Should Use It? */}
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">01 / Overview</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-bold">What Does This Calculator Measure and Who Should Use It?</h2>
      <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
        The <strong>Instagram Engagement Rate Calculator</strong> measures the percentage of an audience that actively interacts with a post relative to a defined baseline—either total account followers or unique accounts reached. While follower count reflects potential distribution scale, engagement rate reveals true audience resonance, content retention, and algorithmic health.
      </p>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
        <div class="p-5 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2 shadow-2xs">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-ink font-semibold">
            <span class="text-base">🎨</span>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold">Content Creators</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Diagnose which post formats (Reels vs. Carousels) convert viewers into interactions. Prove audience engagement in media kits with verified metrics rather than raw follower counts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2 shadow-2xs">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-ink font-semibold">
            <span class="text-base">📊</span>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold">Social Media Managers</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Track month-over-month account health, detect audience fatigue or inactive follower drag, and benchmark client content performance against realistic tier standards.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2 shadow-2xs">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-ink font-semibold">
            <span class="text-base">💼</span>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold">Brands & Marketers</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Audit influencer candidates before signing sponsorship agreements, screen out bot-inflated profiles, and calculate exact Cost-Per-Engagement (CPE) for campaign post-mortems.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 2: Supported Calculation Methods & Verified Formulas */}
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">02 / Formulas & Methodology</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-bold">Supported Calculation Methods: ERR vs. ERF</h2>
      <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
        The calculator implements two distinct, mathematically sound calculation methods based directly on your choice of denominator. Understanding which denominator to use is essential for accurate performance analysis:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {/* ERR Card */}
        <div id="err-formula-card" class="p-6 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border-2 border-primary space-y-3 transition-all shadow-xs">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider">Method 1: Reach-Based</h3>
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold bg-primary/10 text-primary rounded-pill">ERR</span>
          </div>
          <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Engagement Rate by Reach</h4>
          <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg font-mono text-xs text-ink border border-hairline">
            ERR = (Total Engagements / Accounts Reached) × 100
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <strong>What it evaluates:</strong> How effectively a post converted <em>actual viewers</em> into active participants. Because it divides by unique people reached (from Instagram Insights), it is completely immune to inactive or ghost followers on your profile.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <strong>Best used for:</strong> Optimizing individual Reels, testing opening visual hooks, and evaluating non-follower Explore page distribution.
          </p>
        </div>

        {/* ERF Card */}
        <div id="erf-formula-card" class="p-6 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-3 transition-all opacity-80 shadow-xs">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Method 2: Follower-Based</h3>
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold bg-surface-strong text-muted rounded-pill">ERF</span>
          </div>
          <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Engagement Rate by Followers</h4>
          <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg font-mono text-xs text-ink border border-hairline">
            ERF = (Total Engagements / Total Followers) × 100
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <strong>What it evaluates:</strong> How actively your total public follower base responds to your content. Because follower count and public likes/comments are visible without private dashboard access, ERF is the primary standard for external account screening.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <strong>Best used for:</strong> Baseline profile audits, media kit overviews, and monitoring macro audience retention over 6–12 months.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Supporting Ratio Calculations */}
      <div class="p-5 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>⚡</span> Supporting Algorithmic Intent Signals
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          In addition to overall engagement rate, the tool computes two critical ratio metrics whenever Likes are greater than zero:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-1">
          <div class="p-3.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft space-y-1">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>🔖</span> Save-to-Like Ratio = (Saves / Likes) × 100
            </span>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
              Measures evergreen utility. A ratio above 15% indicates that users consider the post a valuable reference worth returning to later (infographics, recipes, tutorials).
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft space-y-1">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>🚀</span> Share-to-Like Ratio = (Shares / Likes) × 100
            </span>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
              Measures viral velocity. A ratio above 20% indicates strong word-of-mouth endorsement, alerting Instagram's recommendation system to distribute the post to Explore and non-followers.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Comparison Table */}
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-surface-card shadow-xs">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-canvas-soft border-b border-hairline text-ink font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">Comparison Dimension</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5 text-primary font-bold">Reach-Based (ERR)</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">Follower-Based (ERF)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline-soft text-body">
            <tr class="hover:bg-canvas-soft/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink">Denominator</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-primary font-medium">Accounts Reached (Private Insights)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Total Followers (Public Profile)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-canvas-soft/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink">Primary Analytical Focus</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-primary font-medium">Creative resonance & viewer hook conversion</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Overall account authority & follower affinity</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-canvas-soft/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink">Ghost Follower Distortion</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">Zero impact (only measures active viewers)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-red-500 font-medium">Penalized by dormant or inactive followers</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-canvas-soft/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink">Viral Reach Behavior</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">Normalizes rate cleanly across high reach</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-medium">Can spike well over 100% on breakout Reels</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-canvas-soft/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink">Data Requirement</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Requires access to post Insights tab</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">Publicly verifiable without login</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 3: Supported Inputs vs. Unsupported Metrics */}
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">03 / Accepted Inputs</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-bold">Metrics Accepted by This Calculator</h2>
      <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
        To avoid misleading calculations, this tool accepts only verified, standard metrics provided directly by Instagram's native interface. We do not inflate results or introduce unsupported variables:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="p-4 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span class="text-primary font-bold">✓</span> Supported Inputs
          </h3>
          <ul class="text-xs text-muted space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4 leading-relaxed">
            <li><strong>Total Followers:</strong> Profile audience count; used as the denominator for ERF and tier benchmarks.</li>
            <li><strong>Accounts Reached:</strong> Unique accounts that viewed the post (from Instagram Insights); used as denominator for ERR.</li>
            <li><strong>Likes:</strong> Double-tap heart interactions on the post.</li>
            <li><strong>Comments:</strong> Public text replies left on the post.</li>
            <li><strong>Shares / Sends:</strong> Direct Message forwards and external shares.</li>
            <li><strong>Saves:</strong> Bookmarks saved to private collections.</li>
            <li><strong>Total Engagements:</strong> Automatically calculated sum: <code>Likes + Comments + Shares + Saves</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span class="text-red-500 font-bold">✗</span> Unsupported Metrics (Excluded by Design)
          </h3>
          <ul class="text-xs text-muted space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4 leading-relaxed">
            <li><strong>Impressions:</strong> Total views including repeat views by the same account. Impressions are not used because repeat views artificially deflate engagement percentages.</li>
            <li><strong>Story Sticker Taps & Polls:</strong> Ephemeral interactions specific to Stories, which follow separate 24-hour expiration models.</li>
            <li><strong>Profile Visits & Bio Link Clicks:</strong> Navigational actions rather than on-post content interactions.</li>
            <li><strong>Direct Messages / Private Chats:</strong> Private communication outside public post feeds.</li>
            <li><strong>Automated API Sync:</strong> We do not ask for Instagram credentials or run automated scrapers; all entries are calculated client-side in your browser.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 4: Manually Verified Worked Examples */}
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">04 / Worked Examples</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-bold">Manually Verified Worked Examples</h2>
      <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
        Review these two realistic publishing scenarios showing exact inputs, step-by-step arithmetic, and strategic interpretations:
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        {/* Example 1 */}
        <div class="p-6 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-4 shadow-2xs">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-hairline-soft pb-3">
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Example 1: Breakout Educational Reel (Micro Creator)</span>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-0.5">A 24,000-follower creator publishes a tutorial Reel picked up by the Explore algorithm.</p>
            </div>
            <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-pill bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-semibold text-xs border border-emerald-500/20">
              High Reach Conversion
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-6 gap-2.5 font-mono text-xs">
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Followers</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">24,000</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Reach</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">68,000</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Likes</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">2,750</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Comments</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">180</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Shares</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">1,420</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Saves</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">850</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-3 pt-1 text-xs">
            <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline text-ink leading-relaxed font-mono">
              <strong>Step 1: Calculate Total Engagements</strong><br />
              Total = 2,750 (Likes) + 180 (Comments) + 1,420 (Shares) + 850 (Saves) = <strong>5,200 Engagements</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <div class="p-3.5 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 text-ink space-y-1.5">
                <strong class="text-primary block font-semibold">Reach-Based Calculation (ERR):</strong>
                <code class="block font-mono">(5,200 / 68,000) × 100 = 7.647% &rarr; <strong>7.65% ERR</strong></code>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-muted leading-normal">
                  <strong>Interpretation:</strong> Converted 7.65% of unique viewers into an active interaction. This strongly exceeds the Micro tier average (2.5%–4.5%), confirming exceptional hook retention.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-3.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline text-ink space-y-1.5">
                <strong class="text-muted block font-semibold">Follower-Based Calculation (ERF):</strong>
                <code class="block font-mono">(5,200 / 24,000) × 100 = 21.666% &rarr; <strong>21.67% ERF</strong></code>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-muted leading-normal">
                  <strong>Interpretation:</strong> The 21.67% ERF reflects viral distribution where post reach (68,000) was 2.83× higher than total followers (24,000). ERF highlights viral reach multiplier effects.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft text-[11px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Intent Signal Check:</strong> Share-to-Like ratio reached <strong>51.64%</strong> (1,420 / 2,750), and Save-to-Like ratio reached <strong>30.91%</strong> (850 / 2,750). These high signals explain why Instagram's recommendation engine continued pushing the Reel to non-followers.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* Example 2 */}
        <div class="p-6 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-4 shadow-2xs">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-hairline-soft pb-3">
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Example 2: In-Feed Sponsored Carousel (Mid-Tier Creator)</span>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-0.5">An 85,000-follower creator publishes a 7-slide educational carousel for a brand campaign.</p>
            </div>
            <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-pill bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-semibold text-xs border border-blue-500/20">
              High Utility & Saves
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-6 gap-2.5 font-mono text-xs">
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Followers</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">85,000</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Reach</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">18,200</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Likes</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">640</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Comments</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">48</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Shares</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">35</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft">
              <span class="text-muted text-[10px] block font-sans">Saves</span>
              <span class="text-ink font-bold">147</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-3 pt-1 text-xs">
            <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline text-ink leading-relaxed font-mono">
              <strong>Step 1: Calculate Total Engagements</strong><br />
              Total = 640 (Likes) + 48 (Comments) + 35 (Shares) + 147 (Saves) = <strong>870 Engagements</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <div class="p-3.5 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 text-ink space-y-1.5">
                <strong class="text-primary block font-semibold">Reach-Based Calculation (ERR):</strong>
                <code class="block font-mono">(870 / 18,200) × 100 = 4.780% &rarr; <strong>4.78% ERR</strong></code>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-muted leading-normal">
                  <strong>Interpretation:</strong> Among the 18,200 people who actually saw the post, engagement was 4.78%. This outperforms the Mid-Tier ERR benchmark (1.8%–3.2%), indicating healthy content resonance.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-3.5 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline text-ink space-y-1.5">
                <strong class="text-muted block font-semibold">Follower-Based Calculation (ERF):</strong>
                <code class="block font-mono">(870 / 85,000) × 100 = 1.023% &rarr; <strong>1.02% ERF</strong></code>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-muted leading-normal">
                  <strong>Interpretation:</strong> ERF appears modest at 1.02%. This is not poor content resonance, but reflects the reality that in-feed carousel reach reached only ~21.4% of total followers (18,200 / 85,000).
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg border border-hairline-soft text-[11px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Strategic Takeaway:</strong> An automated influencer screening platform might flag 1.02% ERF as borderline. However, providing the brand with the 4.78% ERR and high save count (147 saves; 22.97% save-to-like ratio) demonstrates tangible consumer purchase intent and reference value.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 5: Why Engagement Rates Vary */}
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">05 / Analysis Factors</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-bold">Why Engagement Rates Vary Across Accounts</h2>
      <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
        There is no single "universal" engagement rate. Industry benchmark studies (such as annual cross-industry reports from Rival IQ and Sprout Social) confirm that engagement levels fluctuate significantly across four primary variables:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 pt-1">
        <div class="p-4 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>📉</span> 1. Audience Scale (The Size Penalty)
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Follower-based engagement rate (ERF) naturally decreases as an account grows. Nano and micro creators enjoy high community intimacy where a large fraction of followers see and comment on every post. When an account expands past 100,000 followers, Instagram distributes content across broader, more passive audience segments, pulling average ERF down toward 0.5%–1.5%.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>🎬</span> 2. Content Format & Algorithm Goals
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Each format serves a different distribution purpose. <strong>Reels</strong> are optimized for non-follower discovery, driving massive reach and higher share velocity. <strong>Carousels</strong> encourage extended dwell time and command the highest average save rates. <strong>Static photos</strong> deliver quick double-tap likes but lower bookmark utility.
          </p>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-muted">
            <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Creator Tip:</span> If your Reels suffer from low view-to-engagement rates, verify that native app icons and captions aren't obscuring your visual hooks using our free <a href="/instagram-reels-overlay-tester" class="text-primary font-semibold hover:underline">Instagram Reels Safe Zone Overlay Tester</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>🏢</span> 3. Industry Niche & Audience Intent
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            High-emotion, lifestyle, fitness, and entertainment niches experience spontaneous double-tap likes and comments. In contrast, technical B2B, finance, legal, or educational accounts typically exhibit lower visible like counts but significantly higher saves and private DM forwards per viewer reached.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-surface-card rounded-xl border border-hairline space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>📐</span> 4. Measurement Methodology
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Comparing an account's reach-based rate (ERR) against another's follower-based rate (ERF) produces an invalid comparison. Because reach is often a fraction of follower count on static posts—or multiple times higher on viral Reels—the resulting rates can differ by 5x to 10x for the exact same post. Always establish the denominator before comparing metrics.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
